cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this repository helps you, you may cite it as below. It is an informal,
  work-in-progress synthesis of published research, written with Claude, an AI
  assistant by Anthropic. It is not an official standard, not peer-reviewed,
  and not a new result.
title: "ai-augmented-data-gathering (work in progress)"
abstract: >-
  The most efficient way to gather data in general, information foraging first: foraging models, the stopping estimator for what is still unseen, the choice of the next source as a bandit, and the value of information for a dear source, as programs the reviews can run. Scope only; the review is not started.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tewf"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tewf/ai-augmented-data-gathering"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - information foraging
  - optimal stopping
  - species richness
  - multi-armed bandit
  - value of information
  - literature review
